      "finite_search_hypothesis": "R_nodes: one eligible adjacent or active-reflection node defined below, for p=(2,3,q), q∈{23,29,31}, b∈{0,…,15}³, has G>0. R_nodes is a prospective search hypothesis, not an assumption of the proof. Failure of this finite search does not refute R or prove C.",
      "non_binding_fact": "R: there exist k≥3, distinct actual prime labels, nonnegative integer exponents, and two distinct actual exponent configurations in a closed slab with log(5040)<T₀<T₁, satisfying every definition and support condition of C, with G>0. This is the proposed new arithmetic fact, currently unverified; the intended public theorem is result : Not C."
    },
    "question": {
      "complete_chosen_statement": "Let C be the closed proposition: for every integer k≥3, every p:Fin k→N of pairwise distinct primes, every b:Fin k→N (zero exponents included), and every pair of finite real budgets log(5040)<T₀<T₁, if there exist distinct a,a′:Fin k→N with a_i,a′_i∈{b_i,b_i+1} and both T₀≤Σ_i a_i log p_i≤T₁ and T₀≤Σ_i a′_i log p_i≤T₁, then U_dual≤U_var, with the following exact definitions and valid-domain qualifications. Put h_i=log p_i, c_i=(b_i+1)h_i, d_i=(b_i+2)h_i, Q=Σ_i h_i, M_j=T_j+Q, f(x)=log(1−exp(−x)) on x>0, μ=M₁/k, I=[M₀/k,M₁/k], V₀=Σ_i dist(I,{c_i,d_i})², r=sqrt(V₀/[k(k−1)]), L=μ−r, H=μ+(k−1)r. Distance is inf{|x−y|:x∈I,y∈{c_i,d_i}}; V₀ has no further division by k. Retain μ>0, 0≤V₀<k(k−1)μ² and L>0 (the source derives these from an actual admitted positive corner; they may not be silently presumed for an arbitrary grid). E=∏_i(1−1/p_i)^(−1). D=inf_{λ≥0}(λM₁+Σ_i max(f(c_i)−λc_i,f(d_i)−λd_i)); Ψ=f(H)+(k−1)f(L); U_dual=log E+D and U_var=log E+Ψ. Thus C asserts G=D−Ψ≤0. The equivalent fractional primal maximizes Σ_i[(1−y_i)f(c_i)+y_i f(d_i)] over 0≤y_i≤1, Σ_i h_i y_i≤M₁−Σ_i c_i, with no lower-budget constraint. Endpoint inclusion, zero radius, price ties and all finite upper slack retain their definitions. In a matching optimum with exactly one truly fractional row j, x_j=(1−θ)c_j+θd_j and other x_i actual endpoints, J_j=f(x_j)−(1−θ)f(c_j)−θf(d_j)>0 and G=Σ_i f(x_i)−Ψ−J_j. This residual identity does not supply its sign or a general equality classification.",
      "exact_search_domain": {
        "box_window": "p=(2,3,23),(2,3,29),(2,3,31); each b_i∈{0,…,15}. Do not replace the universal C by this window in a deliverable.",
        "layout_only": "12,288 boxes; at most 25 raw slots per box, 307,200 raw slots before guards; at most six permutation fills per active node. These are source-derived layout counts, not runtime, evaluated-case counts, certified exclusions or numeric ROI.",
        "nodes": "For each box let P=∏p_i and let R₀<…<R₇ be the eight distinct integers ∏p_i^(b_i+e_i), with masks e∈{0,1}³ sorted by exact integer comparison. β_s=log(P R_s). Adjacent slots s=1,…,7 use (M₀,M₁)=(β_{s−1},β_s) with R_{s−1}>5040. Reflection slots j=1,…,6 and i=0,1,2 use X=P R_{j−1}, E_i=p_i^[3(2b_i+3)], (M₀,M₁)=(log X,log(E_i/X)), only if R_{j−1}>5040, p_i^[3(b_i+1)]<X, X²<E_i, and P²R_{j−1}R_j<E_i<P²R_{j−1}R_{j+1}. Their original budgets are T₀=log R_{j−1}, T₁=log(E_i/(P²R_{j−1})). Every guard is exact; the reflection upper exponential is a positive noninteger rational, not an integer corner.",
